-------+---------------------+----------+--------------------------------------------------------
 31337 | idle in transaction | 00:03:02 | SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE
```

Statement: "`SELECT pg_cancel_backend(31337);` releases the row lock: it cancels the session''s transaction."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. `pg_cancel_backend` cancels the query that is running; an idle-in-transaction session runs none, so nothing happens and the lock stays. `pg_terminate_backend(31337)` ends the session, which rolls the transaction back and frees the lock. `idle_in_transaction_session_timeout` does the same automatically. The real bug is in the app: it called the payment provider while holding the transaction open.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_121') AND order_index = 1)
