Statement: "For the whole rollout, old and new pods serve requests against the same database, so any schema change that runs before or during it has to work with both versions of the code."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. A rolling update replaces pods a few at a time; for minutes both versions handle traffic. The migration runs once, before or at the start of the rollout, so the schema it leaves behind must satisfy the old code (still reading and writing `customer_phone`) and the new code (using `phone_e164`). That is what the expand step guarantees; the contract step waits for a later release, when no old pod is left.', 2, 5
