    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_141'), 'The team now runs every migration with a lock timeout and retries:

```text
migrate  SET lock_timeout = ''3s''
migrate  ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN tip_vnd integer DEFAULT 0
migrate  ERROR:  canceling statement due to lock timeout
migrate  attempt 1 failed, retrying in 20s
migrate  ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN tip_vnd integer DEFAULT 0
migrate  ALTER TABLE  (Time: 2.871 ms)
```

Statement: "The `ALTER TABLE` gave up after waiting 3 seconds for its lock instead of making every query queue behind it for minutes; the retry found a moment when no conflicting lock was held."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. `lock_timeout` aborts a statement that waits longer than the limit to acquire a lock. Other queries can queue behind it for those 3 seconds at most, and the migration tool tries again later, when the long query has finished. The timeout must be short enough that 3 seconds of queued queries are acceptable; `statement_timeout` alone does not help, because it also counts the work, not only the wait.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_141') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
)
